# HeaderRow

`HeaderRow` represents the model of a `<tr>` element in `<thead>`.

## Usage

### `id: string`

A constant `id` that uniquely identifies the header row.

### `current: { attrs: HeaderRowAttributes; props: HeaderRowProps }`

The attributes and plugin props of the `<tr>` element as plain reactive values. `current.attrs` is ready to spread onto the element; `current.props` holds each plugin's props, keyed by plugin name. Both update in place as table and plugin state change. Reads outside a template or effect return the current value, and server rendering produces the same markup.

```svelte
<tr {...headerRow.current.attrs}>
```

<Admonition type="tip">See also <a href="/docs/plugins/overview">Plugin View Model Extensions</a>. v7 removed the <code>attrs()</code> and <code>props()</code> store methods; see <a href="/docs/guides/migrating-to-v7">Migrating to v7</a>.</Admonition>

### `cells: HeaderCell[]`

An array of <a href="./header-cell">`HeaderCell`</a>s to iterate over and apply onto `<th>` elements.

`cells` only includes the cells of <strong>visible columns</strong>.


